        "CVE-2023-38408": {
            "cveID": "CVE-2023-38408",
            "confidences": [
                {
                    "score": 100,
                    "detectionMethod": "OpenSSHExactVersionMatch"
                }
            ],
            "distroAdvisories": [
                {
                    "advisoryID": "OPENSSH-2023-07-19-1",
                    "severity": "",
                    "issued": "2023-07-19T00:00:00Z",
                    "updated": "1000-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                    "description": "ssh-agent(1) in OpenSSH between 5.5 and 9.3p1 (inclusive) remote code execution relating to PKCS#11 providers\n\nThe PKCS#11 support ssh-agent(1) could be abused to achieve remote code execution via a forwarded agent socket if the following conditions are met:\n\nExploitation requires the presence of specific libraries on the victim system.\n\nRemote exploitation requires that the agent was forwarded to an attacker-controlled system.\n\nExploitation can also be prevented by starting ssh-agent(1) with an empty PKCS#11/FIDO allowlist (ssh-agent -P '') or by configuring an allowlist that contains only specific provider libraries.\n\nThis vulnerability was discovered and demonstrated to be exploitable by the Qualys Security Advisory team. This vulnerability has been assigned CVE-2023-38408.\n\nThis bug is corrected in OpenSSH 9.3p2. For OpenBSD, an errata patch exists to fix this problem.\n\nFor more information, please refer to the release notes."
                }
            ],
